</h3><ul><li>24 chocolate sandwich cookies</li><li>5 tbsp melted butter</li><li>24 large marshmallows (about 6 oz)</li><li>1/2 cup whole milk</li><li>1 tsp peppermint extract</li><li>2–3 drops green food coloring, optional</li><li>1 1/4 cups heavy whipping cream, divided</li><li>1/2 cup mini chocolate chips or finely chopped semisweet chocolate</li><li>2 tbsp powdered sugar</li><li>Chocolate shavings for topping</li></ul></div><div><h3>Step-by-step</h3><ol><li>Crush cookies finely and combine with melted butter. Press into a 9-inch pie plate. Chill 20 minutes.</li><li>Combine marshmallows and milk in a saucepan over low heat. Stir constantly until the marshmallows are completely melted and the mixture is smooth. Do not boil.</li><li>Remove from heat and stir in peppermint extract and optional food coloring. Cool to room temperature, stirring occasionally so a skin does not form.</li><li>Whip 1 cup heavy cream to stiff peaks.</li><li>Fold the whipped cream into the cooled mint-marshmallow mixture in three additions, keeping as much air as possible.</li><li>Fold in mini chocolate chips.</li><li>Spread into the crust and chill at least 6 hours, preferably overnight.</li><li>Before serving, whip the remaining 1/4 cup cream with powdered sugar and spoon or pipe it on top. Finish with chocolate shavings.</li></ol></div></div><div class="note"><strong>KaySo note:</strong> Classic marshmallow-and-whipped-cream grasshopper pie. For a firmer slice, freeze it 2–3 hours and let it soften 10 minutes before serving.</div><div class="recipe-actions"><button data-share-recipe>↗ Share Recipe</button><button data-copy-recipe>Copy Recipe</button><span class="status"></span></div></div></details></main><div class="footer">Packers Game Day Recipe Book</div><script src="../recipes.js"></script></body></html>